//! The diacritic-folding table from the reference `remove_diacritics`.
//!
//! Machine-derived from the reference tables; do not edit by hand.
//!
//! The reference stores 86 `{ base, letters: /[...]/g }` rules and runs 86
//! sequential global-regex passes. Because every replacement is an ASCII letter
//! and every ASCII letter is itself a key mapping to itself, no pass can cascade
//! into another, so the whole thing collapses to one left-to-right per-`char`
//! lookup. The generator re-proves that equivalence on every run — exhaustively
//! over all 63,488 non-surrogate BMP codepoints and over 20,000 random strings —
//! and refuses to emit a table if it ever fails.
//!
//! The 52 ASCII identity entries are omitted: [`super::remove_diacritics`]
//! short-circuits on `is_ascii`, which is both faster and exactly equivalent.

